  "worked_solution": "First, we write our system in matrix form as $Ax=b,$ where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 14 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe normal equation corresponding to $Ax=b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}7 & 14 \\\\ 2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 14 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 14 \\\\ 2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}245 & 70 & 35 \\\\ 70 & 20 & 10 \\\\ 35 & 10 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}35 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=35+10+35=80.\n$$",
